4. Sri B.S.Shivaji, learned counsel appearing for the petitioner- accused No. 2, submits that the petitioner is working as Project Director, NHAI, Project Implementation Unit, Nellore; that on 12-07-2001, a notification was issued under Section 3 A of the Act proposing to widen the highway from two lanes to four lanes between Chilakaluripet and Nellore; that as the land of respondent No.
1 in an extent of Ac. 0.00  cent along with structures thereon is passing through the alignment of the road widening, NHAI issued a notification for acquiring of the said land and structures thereon;
that after thoroughly following the procedure, an award was passed on 15-07-2002 in favour of respondent No. 1 for an amount of Rs.87,749/- towards acquisition of land and structures thereon and the same was paid to respondent No. 1 by way of cheque bearing No. 487416 dated 15-07-2002;
that in the year 2009, for the second phase of road widening from four lanes to six lanes, NHAI issued another notification dated 30-11-2009 under Section 3 A of the Act; that in the second phase,
an extent of 20.24 square meters of land belonging to respondent No. 1 was acquired and an award dated 19-04-2012 was passed granting compensation of Rs.7,000/- to respondent No. 1 but respondent No. 1 refused to receive the same and that as the structures were already acquired by NHAI and compensation was also paid during the first phase of widening, question of demolishing the structures again does not arise during the second phase.
